---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import legacyPages from '../../data/legacy-pages.json';
const page = legacyPages['blogs-serving-notice'];
---

<SiteLayout {...page} legacy={true} noindex={false}>
  <main id="main" class="article-content">
    <nav class="article-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/blogs/"
        >Hiring &amp; career guides</a
      >
    </nav><p class="overline">Quantum Leaps · Practical guidance</p><h1>
      Serving Notice: Finish Well and Prepare for What’s Next
    </h1><p class="article-meta">
      By Quantum Leaps · Published and reviewed 25 October 2026 · 2 min read
    </p><p class="article-note">
      A practical handover and joining checklist that respects both your current
      and future teams.
    </p><h2>Confirm the dates</h2><p>
      Discuss your contractual notice, leave balance, handover responsibilities
      and proposed last working day with the appropriate person at your
      employer. Keep your future employer informed of confirmed dates, and
      distinguish requests from approvals.
    </p><h2>Make the handover usable</h2><p>
      Document current work, owners, deadlines and known risks in the systems
      your team uses. Share access through approved company processes. Do not
      forward private client files or internal credentials to a personal
      account.
    </p><h2>Prepare without working two jobs</h2><p>
      Ask your future manager about onboarding, equipment and introductory
      reading. Any pre-joining contact should respect your current obligations.
      Do not perform confidential work for a future employer while creating a
      conflict with your current role.
    </p><h2>Keep communication clear</h2><ul>
      <li>Confirm your last working day and joining date in writing.</li><li>
        Keep the recruiter informed about material changes.
      </li><li>
        Discuss references and permission before sharing contact details.
      </li><li>Retain your own permitted employment documents.</li><li>
        Check where and when to arrive, or how remote onboarding works.
      </li>
    </ul><p>
      A considered transition protects professional relationships and helps the
      next team prepare.
    </p><p>
      <a href="/contact/">Discuss a hiring brief →</a> · <a href="/submit-cv/"
        >Share your CV →</a
      >
    </p>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
